om  gringotts on top of a dragon it seems  like there couldn't be any better  feeling in the world  shortly after the fact when they get  dropped into a lake  well this wasn't a scene that had the  actors feeling particularly good since  later in the movie the actors have to  change they weren't able to wear any  layers underneath their clothing to keep  warm after plunging into a frigid lake  the filming for this scene took place  deep in the winter months we're talking  january february  so the water was unbearably freezing to  make it that much worse the water in the  lake couldn't be heated at all either so  the actors had to struggle trying to  perform and breathe normally in these  trying conditions for watson it was one  of the absolute worst experiences she  had filming rupert grint actually  struggled so much at one point he was  terrified because he felt as if his  heart had stopped beating  if anything he feels more dangerous just  watching harry potter and the goblet of  fire is an intense experience  we absolutely feel for the actors who  had to deal with rough weather daring  stunts and extremely emotional scenes  for radcliffe the worst scenes to film  for the fourth installment were the ones  underwater as part of the triwizard  tournament to prepare for these daring  scenes radcliffe had to undergo intense  diving lessons to make sure he could  perform what was needed as safely as  possible the stress didn't end there  though  unfortunately it took a full six weeks  of torture to finally capture all the  footage that was needed for the movie in  total radcliffe dealt with a full 41  hours underwater filming that amount of  time in combination with the freezing  temperatures were pretty rough on the  actor physically radcliffe wound up  suffering two bad ear infections as a  result of the rough filming conditions a  bit frustrating was the fact that  communication is obviously quite  difficult while daniel radcliffe played  a total quidditch star he 