 to do it  even though the content was pretty  incredible well done everyone great  great work we all love to hate dolores  umbridge and while the actress plays the  cruel and vicious woman extremely  convincingly the performance came at a  cost imelda staunton loved working on  the franchise but after filming  intensely mean scenes she didn't always  feel very good one scene in particular  put her over the edge  the actress was left feeling really  awful for a couple of days after filming  this scene with the most painful line  session we've ever seen  you deserve to be punished it was a  really disturbing moment for staunton  when she realized people could be  capable of such vile behavior for some  actors filming deeply cruel and vicious  content can be seriously tough mentally  because she's  quite hard bonnie wright of course had  to lock lips with daniel radcliffe but  when it came to filming their kissing  scenes in particular their first in the  sixth film wright felt a lot of  uncomfortable pressure performing what  was meant to be a pretty significant  moment combine that with the awkwardness  of kissing someone who's more like  family in front of a crowd of people who  are filming your every move let's just  say kissing harry unfortunately wasn't  the most fun scene for the actress to  film just like any other scene that  you're filming so acting legend day  maggie smith had her fair share of  difficult experiences behind the scenes  on the harry potter set  the actress had to endure acting and  sitting in huge heavy costumes heavy  hats were the cherry on top of the  annoying experience  what made it all worse is that sometimes  she'd prepare to film a scene in full  costume hair and makeup but they  wouldn't get to her so all that duress  was for nothing not to mention the fact  that smith also underwent cancer  treatments while filming some of the  movies  talk about a trooper no one can mess  with mcgonagall is it's magic  adolescence is tough for any teenager  but poor matthew lewis had to deal with  being a teenager and made to look  supremely awkward and nerdy various  movies saw lewis in a fat suit false  teeth and bits of plastic behind his  ears to make them stick out being on set  and filming made the actor very  self-conscious  particularly once he was a bit older and  was more attuned to the fact that there  were lots of girls on set who only ever  saw him as nerdy neville it was horrible  while we gushed watching hermione and  ron finally kiss the two actors weren't  feeling nearly as good about the whole  situation the pair of course have a  sibling-like relationship having grown  up together so performing this intimate  and passionate kiss in front of loads of  people who they'd also known for years  was a nightmare  that wasn't the only awkward kiss though  watson and radcliffe had to share a  steamy smooch as well which was made  even worse to film by the presence of  rupert grint the actor's laughter didn't  last for long though since it was so  distracting watson actually had grint  kicked off of the set  helen and bonham carter gives an  extraordinary performance as the evil  bellatrix but when she was on set things  sometimes went a bit too far leaving the  actress with some regrettable memories  bonham carter wound up badly injuring  her co-star matthew lewis when she  perforated his eardrum during a scene  leaving him with internal bleeding while  the scene looks great in the movie it  wasn't so fun for the actress to film we  can't imagine it was matthew lewis's  favorite either everyone had their  different styles of one fighting  could there be anything more chilling  than an embrace from he who shall not be  named  tom felton was totally taken off guard  by this improvised move from voldemort  actor ray fines which left him feeling  really uncomfortable the whole scene had  felt in on edge confused and a little  terrified by the creepy hug  well done  while the banquet scenes in the first  film looked regal and decadent filming  them was far from pleasant for the  actors if we could smell what was on  film audiences would have been running  out of the theater because the food  being filmed had been rotting for days  as the days went on shooting these  scenes became nauseating for the actors  who had to deal with the stench of food  going bad only made worse by being under  hot lights for hours on end i'll say one  two three in action the food appears who  knew filming such a beloved series could  have been so difficult for the actors  knowing just how big a struggle these  scenes were for the performers in real  life totally changes our perspective of  their performances with such pros it's  no surprise they were so often able to  act through their discomfort  which scene sounded toughest to you

